# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Environment — copy this file to `.env` and fill it in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env        (macOS / Linux / Git Bash)
#   copy .env.example .env      (Windows CMD)
#   Copy-Item .env.example .env (Windows PowerShell)
#
# `.env` is git-ignored. NEVER commit a key.
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Google Maps SDK for Android.
#
# How to get one:
#   1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick)
#      a project. Billing must be ENABLED on the project — the Maps
#      SDK for Android requires it — but the free tier covers 28,000
#      map loads a month, so a demo app costs nothing.
#   2. Enable "Maps SDK for Android" under APIs & Services → Library.
#   3. Create an API key under Credentials → Create credentials →
#      API key.
#   4. RESTRICT the key: Android apps → package name
#      `com.codenzic.wayfare` + your signing SHA-1. Do not leave the
#      key unrestricted.
#   5. Paste it below.
#
# Without a key the route screen still builds and runs, but the map
# area renders Google's grey "authorisation failure" canvas instead
# of tiles.
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=
